WEB SOURCE (the specification — read end to end)
  web/src/components/forms/TreeSelect.tsx (+ __tests__/TreeSelect.test.tsx). A generic tri-state
  two-level tree multi-select primitive:
    • Two-level hierarchy (groups -> leaves) with tri-state group checkboxes (none / partial / all).
    • In-component search filter that FILTERS the tree (does not flatten): a group whose own label
      matches keeps all its leaves, else only matching leaves; zero-match groups drop.
    • Selection is INDEPENDENT of the filter: a selected leaf stays selected when filtered out of
      view; group / "select visible" actions only ever touch currently-visible leaves.
    • Group + top-level toggles act on VISIBLE, ENABLED leaves only (disabled leaves never auto-
      select and never block the "all selected" determination).
    • Per-group `{selected}/{visible}` counts; top-level "Select all" / "Clear all" that flips to
      "Select N visible" / "Clear N visible" while searching; "Clear all selected" link.
    • Right-slot `renderLeafRight` / `renderGroupRight` (badges, sparklines); per-leaf disabled +
      reason; controlled selection / expansion / search; loading skeleton; empty + no-results states.
    • WAI-ARIA tree pattern + roving-tabindex keyboard nav (Arrow / Home / End / Space / Enter),
      aria-checked "true|mixed|false", sr-only live summary.
    • The functional-setter onChange so rapid successive toggles accumulate (no stale-closure clobber).
  Data sources (prompt): `useId` only — the primitive is controlled, no HTTP. The native surface
  binds the catalog through the shared P1/S8 state-holder seam; selection/search/expansion are owned
  locally by the observable model.

